SPEC = {'file': 'cover_innocent_business_analyst', 'label': 'innocent drinks Business Analyst', 'center': True, 'paras': ['I am writing to apply for the Business Analyst talent pool at innocent drinks. I am completing an MSc in Health Data Science at University College London, where a distinction is expected, after a BSc in Biological Sciences at Imperial College London, and I currently work as a Data Analyst Intern at TikTok Shop UK. This role is close to what I have actually done: working with teams to understand how their work is done, turning their questions into clear problems, and recommending changes they can act on.', 'What attracts me most to innocent is that data is used to grow the business responsibly, and that analysts work with people as much as numbers. As a B Corp that wants to help people eat more fruit and vegetables, innocent combines a commercial business with a purpose I care about. I enjoy taking an unclear business problem, identifying what users actually need, and turning it into a workflow that can be tested and improved.', 'At TikTok Shop UK I am a Data Analyst Intern, where I analyse merchant and transaction data in SQL and Python and build the KPI frameworks and dashboards that operations, product and commercial teams use to set targets and track initiatives. Alongside my analytical work I built an AI agent that automates repetitive steps of the analytics workflow, which has been adopted by my own team and by partner teams. Building it meant understanding an existing workflow in detail, deciding which steps to automate, and then supporting colleagues as they began to rely on it. I use Claude Code in my development work and review the code it produces rather than accepting it unchecked.', 'At Ipsos Strategy3 I turned more than 80 healthcare professional interviews into quantitative insight through a structured coding framework, built market-sizing models, and worked with the research and strategy teams to turn the findings into recommendations for clients. At DS Digital Technology I also worked as a Data Scientist Intern on a medical AI engagement, where I built Python pipelines that called six LLM APIs with retrieval and multi-step workflows and automated the processing and scoring of over 2,400 records. I designed the evaluation framework around it, a 246-question benchmark and a six-dimension rubric that the client adopted as its acceptance standard, and I co-built a scientifically reviewed knowledge graph and ran blinded A/B tests to measure whether it actually improved output quality.', 'On communication, explaining results clearly to people who do not want the method is something I have done at Ipsos Strategy3 and with pharmaceutical client stakeholders. My dissertation builds predictive and causal models on 458,840 UK Biobank participants and is delivered as a deployed Streamlit application so that people can run scenarios without touching the code.', "Thank you for considering my application. I would welcome the opportunity to discuss how my analytical and stakeholder experience could contribute to innocent's Business Analyst team."]}
